# µ-law audio clips are binary. Without this, core.autocrlf=true (the default
# on the Windows machines this repo is worked on) runs CRLF conversion over
# them: every 0x0D byte that happens to precede a 0x0A is stripped on commit,
# and the corruption is permanent in the object store.
#
# The clips committed on 2026-08-08 contained no 0x0D0A pairs and survived, but
# that is luck — the byte pair is not rare in 8kHz µ-law speech, and the only
# symptom would be a mangled hold phrase on a live patient call.
*.ulaw binary
